==Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
Since 1689 from the dialectal word {{m|sv||vicka|t=yield; bend sideways; run in a waddling fashion}}. Most likely related to {{m|sv|veck|t=a [[fold]]; a [[crease]]}} and {{m|sv|vika|t=to fold}}.

====Verb====
{{sv-verb-reg}}

# [[wiggle]]; [[wobble]]; [[tilt]]
#: {{ux|sv|Hon '''vickade''' på tårna.|She '''wiggled''' her toes.}}
#: {{ux|sv|Om man '''vickar''' på det här locket tillräckligt länge går det av.|If you '''move''' this lid up and down long enough, it will break off.}}
#* {{quote-song|sv|author=w:Caramell|year=2001|album=w:Supergott|trans-album=Super tasty|title=w:Caramelldansen|trans-title=The Caramell dance ("{{l|sv|karamell}}" is the usual spelling)|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H2kdPzjbTkw|text=Så rör på era fötter (o-a-a-a), och '''vicka''' era höfter (o-la-la-la). Gör som vi till denna melodi.|t=So move your feet (o-a-a-a), and '''wiggle''' your hips (o-la-la-la). Do as we do [do as we] to this melody.}}

